data.content:
Three things break in EF Core 10. Here's each issue and its fix:

---

### 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — expression trees no longer accepted

The API now takes a regular `Action` lambda instead of `Expression<Func<...>>`. Your entire expression-tree builder is replaced by simple imperative code:

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

---

### 2. Complex type column name uniquification

Two changes hit you:

- **Same-named properties** across complex types (`ShippingAddress.Street` / `BillingAddress.Street`) now get a numeric suffix automatically (e.g., `Street1`).
- **Nested complex types** use the full path (`Complex_NestedComplex_Property` instead of `NestedComplex_Property`), so `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` becomes `Payment_BillingAddress_City`.

Both generate column-renaming migrations. **Fix:** pin the old names explicitly:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, sa =>
        sa.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, ba =>
        ba.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street"));
});

// For nested complex types:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, p =>
        p.ComplexProperty(pay => pay.BillingAddress, ba =>
            ba.Property(a => a.City).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City")));
});
```

---

### 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

Every method on this interface now has an additional `string logCommandText` parameter (redacted SQL for safe logging). Add it:

```csharp
public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
    IRelationalConnection connection, DbCommand command,
    DbContext context, Guid commandId, Guid connectionId,
    DateTimeOffset startTime,
    string logCommandText)   // ← new parameter
{ /* logging — use logCommandText for safe log output */ }
```

Update all other methods you implement on this interface the same way.
